  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2023-05-10",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would clarify that Australia's civil nuclear power restrictions do not prevent regulators from considering activities involving naval propulsion for conventionally armed nuclear-powered submarines.",
   "It would amend radiation protection and environmental legislation so licensing and approval decisions can be made for relevant naval nuclear propulsion plants and associated activities.",
   "The exceptions would begin the day after Royal Assent, while the civil nuclear moratorium and existing requirements protecting people and the environment would remain."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The radiation safety regulator could issue facility licences involving relevant naval propulsion plants.",
   "The environment minister could make declarations relating to construction or operation of those plants.",
   "Strategic approval and conservation agreement restrictions would also gain naval propulsion exceptions."
  ],
  "affected": "Submarine project proponents, the Australian Radiation Protection and Nuclear Safety Agency and the environment minister are affected.",
